Subject: [PATCH] sched: give disabled WALT header stubs internal linkage

With CONFIG_SCHED_WALT disabled, ThinLTO emits the two externally linked
inline definitions from multiple translation units. Match the neighboring
disabled-feature stubs so a minimal kernel links without WALT.

--- a/include/linux/sched/walt.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched/walt.h
@@ -191,11 +191,11 @@
 {
 }
 
-inline int walt_pause_cpus(struct cpumask *cpus)
+static inline int walt_pause_cpus(struct cpumask *cpus)
 {
 	return 0;
 }
-inline int walt_resume_cpus(struct cpumask *cpus)
+static inline int walt_resume_cpus(struct cpumask *cpus)
 {
 	return 0;
 }
